==================================================
EVIDENCE CLASSES
==================================================

VERIFIED

Direct primary evidence establishes the statement.

Examples:

transaction exists

wallet address interacted

fee value appears in event

block timestamp exists

CORROBORATED

Multiple independent forms of evidence support the statement.

Examples:

RPC event plus explorer receipt

event plus contract-state query

AUTHOR-ORIGINATED

The researcher records a personal observation, decision, or interpretation.

Examples:

“I did not announce the launch before broadcast.”

“I manually approved the transaction.”

PROPOSED

A future methodology or system design has been documented but not yet executed.

FUTURE EXPERIMENT

A hypothesis is awaiting testing.

==================================================
BOT-LIKE CLASSIFICATION FRAMEWORK
==================================================

ROB uses conservative language.

CLASS 0 — UNKNOWN

Insufficient evidence.

CLASS 1 — OPENING-WINDOW PARTICIPANT

The wallet participated within the defined opening period.

No automation claim.

CLASS 2 — AUTOMATED-CANDIDATE

Multiple behavioral signals are consistent with automated execution.

CLASS 3 — REPEATED AUTOMATED-CANDIDATE

The same wallet or behavioral fingerprint appears across independent experiments with repeated characteristics consistent with automation.

CLASS 4 — AUTOMATION CONFIRMED

Independent evidence establishes automated operation.

Do not use CLASS 4 from timing alone.

==================================================
POSSIBLE AUTOMATION SIGNALS
==================================================

Signals may include:

S1 — same-block participation

S2 — extremely low launch-to-trade latency

S3 — repeated first-block participation across launches

S4 — repeated fixed or formulaic trade sizing

S5 — repeated transaction construction

S6 — repeated gas strategy

S7 — repeated entry/exit timing

S8 — repeated interaction with unrelated experimental launches

S9 — recurring participation without corresponding public promotion

S10 — machine-identifiable calling pattern

S11 — independently documented bot infrastructure

No single signal should automatically determine classification.

==================================================
CLASSIFICATION SCORE
==================================================

A research score may be calculated for comparison.

Example conceptual score:

AUTOMATION SCORE

=
TIMING SIGNAL
+
REPETITION SIGNAL
+
TRANSACTION-PATTERN SIGNAL
+
CROSS-LAUNCH SIGNAL
+
INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE SIGNAL

The score is a research heuristic.

It is not proof of identity.

The exact weighting system must be versioned.

Do not silently change weights between experiments.

